A bank account.

An account has an owner (text), a balance (money) and a limit (money).

An account (an account) can pay an amount (money) when:
the amount is at most the account's balance plus the account's limit.

The interest on an account (an account) at a rate (a number) is money:
the account's balance times the rate divided by 100 rounded to 2 places.

Suppose mine is an account with owner "Jose", balance 100 and limit 50.
For example, mine can pay 120.
For example, mine can pay 151 is false.
For example, the interest on mine at 3.5 is 3.5.
